# Configuration for nfo-tracker.service. Edit this, not the unit file.
# Every value below was verified on the development machine; the Zotac will differ in at least
# PYTHON, WORKDIR and the camera serial in CAMERA.

# NOTE: the interpreter and repository paths are gone from here. `pip install .` provides an
# `nfo-tracker` command that does not care about the current directory or PYTHONPATH, and the unit
# invokes it directly. Find its absolute path with `pip show -f nfo-tracker` and put that in
# ExecStart= (systemd will not expand a variable as the command name).

# A STABLE device path, not /dev/videoN. Kernel numbering changes across reboots and replugs -
# on this machine the C920 came up as /dev/video2 while the built-in camera held video0/video1,
# and a reboot can swap them. Verified: cv2 opens this symlink with CAP_V4L2 and negotiates
# 1280x720 MJPG.
#   by-id   = follows THIS camera to any USB port (contains its serial number)
#   by-path = follows THIS USB PORT for any camera - better if the unit may be swapped
# List them with: ls -l /dev/v4l/by-id/ /dev/v4l/by-path/
# NOTE: '-video-index0' is the CAPTURE node. '-index1' is the metadata node and will not stream.
CAMERA=/dev/v4l/by-id/usb-046d_HD_Pro_Webcam_C920_363EAC1F-video-index0
#CAMERA=/dev/v4l/by-path/pci-0000:80:14.0-usb-0:2:1.0-video-index0

# Capture and processing. 1280x720 MJPG @30 is the C920's fastest mode above VGA; in YUYV the
# same camera offers 1080p at 5fps and its maximum 2304x1536 at 2fps, so the format matters more
# than the resolution. --scale halves it again for the tracker: 640x360, ~2.5 ms/frame.
CAM_SIZE=1280x720
CAM_FPS=30
SCALE=0.5

# Seconds between journal status lines (frames, windowed fps, RSS). 300 gives 288 lines/day.
STATUS_EVERY=300

# Optional. Leave empty unless you have a reason: --person-height skips the height bootstrap,
# which otherwise needs someone to walk through frame before tracking starts.
EXTRA_ARGS=
